WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:05.270
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this will
be my Winter Soldier Review.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.920
A lot of you had been asking about it for
a while, but we just got it in the United

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.920
States.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:10.920
Because reasons.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:17.060
Since I this is also my bonus Marvel video
for the week I’ll also talk about how this

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.750
movie impacts what’s going on in the larger
marvel verse.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.420
In case you didn’t know too, Agents of SHIELD
next week will directly follow up on the events

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.400
of this movie, so be sure to subscribe to
get my video.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:31.650
And feel free to leave me suggestions for
future bonus marvel movie videos.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.880
Time to speechify some Winter Soldier.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.329
I’m going to do top 5 moments, my review
and then the interactions with the other movies.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:41.590
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.000
I’ll wait just a sec.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.539
Here we go, Number 5 - The Arnim Zola Reveal

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:50.760
Anyone who’s read the Winter Soldier comic
wasn’t surprised by any of this, but there’s

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.579
a couple reasons why this was awesome and
why it’s really important for what’s going

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:56.070
to happen next year in Age of Ultron.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.590
Toby Stevens is always so much fun to watch,
but it was so funny watching Captain America

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.530
react to him after punching the monitor.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:07.630
That’s one of the things that gets overlooked
when you talk about these kinds of movies.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.630
The humor.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.670
It’s a continuation of the jokes from the
first Avengers movie, Captain America reacting

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.680
to things.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.460
That would make an excellent Fine Brothers
youtube video.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.710
Captain America Reacts to the internet.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:22.280
Of all the things he reacted to, him reacting
to Arnim Zola was one of the best.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.830
The other big thing to take away from this
is the concept of AI in the marvel universe.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.250
I’m talking about Ultron next year.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.910
Arnim Zola basically uploaded his consciousness
into those databanks.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:37.590
Don’t get me started on the plot holes and
why he didn’t jump from system to system,

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:43.400
but think about his algorithm too and how
it relates to Ultron’s core operating mission.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.400
Get rid of all humans.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.520
I’ll talk more about that after my review.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.130
Number 4 - All of the Captain American Winter
Soldier Fight Scenes

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.560
If it wasn’t clear, the Winter Soldier is
also juiced up on super soldier serum.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.360
Not the exact same one Captain America got,
but Bucky is for all intents and purposes,

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.830
just as quick and strong.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:08.110
Watching two super fast super strong people
fight is really hard to pull off without looking

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:11.280
ridiculous, and they did an amazing job.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.700
Think about if from another angle, what if
you and the person you were fighting never

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.599
got tired and were almost indestructible.

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:19.569
Like the Hulk fighting Thor.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:22.640
It could totally look like comedy if your
not careful.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.359
In Avengers they made those two fight and
it was supposed to be funny, like when Hulk

00:02:26.359 --> 00:02:28.150
tried to pick up his hammer.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.200
But in Winter Soldier it’s so much more
personal.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.120
So it’s almost like they’re rolling all
over each other in a wave of steel punches

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.670
and shield bashes.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:43.379
I thought that those fight scenes were way
better than the big CG action scenes at the

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:46.500
end with the helicarriers and Falcon flying
around.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.900
Number 3 - Black Widow Character Development

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:54.310
In case you didn’t know, Black Widow is
probably going to be the first female standalone

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.640
movie they’re going to do.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.640
No release date announced.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.599
But after this movie, she’ll have had more
time baking in the oven than any other female

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:02.980
Marvel character.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.569
As much as I want to see her get a phase 3
movie it feels like Doctor Strange and Black

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:09.579
Panther are the best candidates.

00:03:09.579 --> 00:03:14.330
But it was really the task of this movie to
make her character feel like a real person.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:18.329
In Avengers she had to share screen time with
the Dream Team.

00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:24.040
So with exception to her Hulk and Loki scenes,
she was pretty forgettable along with Hawkeye.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.689
But Winter Soldier felt like a Black Widow
slam dunk.

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:31.420
Scarlett Johansson is a great actress and
I think she got a chance in this movie to

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.810
just be a person as opposed to window dressing.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:41.370
I’ll talk more about her future in the marvelverse
and potential future stories after my review

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.569
too.

00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:46.230
Number 2 - Age of Ultron post credits scene.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.560
The age of miracles.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.159
I loved that Baron Von Strucker line.

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:55.700
He’s treating Hydra the same way Red Skull
treated Hitler and the Nazis.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.249
It’s like he’s playing on a whole other
level.

00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:03.529
When he talked about SHIELD and HYDRA being
two sides of a coin that’s no longer currency

00:04:03.529 --> 00:04:07.680
he was foreshadowing the galactic conflict
that the infinity gems are going to bring.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.750
It was also kind of timely in that we have
the first Galactic Marvel movie coming in

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.750
the fall.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.250
Consider the bar for super hero wow factor
officially raised.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.880
As for the special effects for Quickslilver
and Scarlet Witch, I thought they were interesting.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.200
There have already been a ton of pictures
of them on the set of Age of Ultron.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.560
I’m going to withhold judgement on those
till I see them with completed special effects

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.560
and color grading.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.940
That’s just when they make everything look
all shiny like.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.720
Because Marvel can’t use the word mutant
or Magneto, they’ll be changing their backstories,

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.780
which is a little strange but I’ll wait
to pass judgement till I see the movie.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.290
and my Number 1 - Captain America Destroys
SHIELD

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:51.030
Well he had a little help, but with Nick Fury
going after HYDRA survivors guerilla style

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.810
and everyone kind of going their separate
ways it seems like SHIELD will be in rebuilding

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.830
mode for a long time.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:02.130
Which is the explanation for why they weren’t
in Thor The Dark World or Iron Man 3.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:07.220
They kind of blew up the Triskelion too, so
I think what’s going to happen is Maria

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:11.500
Hill will kind of take over the home base
day to day while Nick Fury is off the grid.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.170
But there’s still all those other SHIELD
agents like Sharon Carter and everyone on

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.170
Agents of SHIELD.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:21.221
I’ll talk more about the blowback from this
as it effects other movie and tv plots, but

00:05:21.221 --> 00:05:25.760
this was such a huge deal I’ll be kind of
pissed if SHIELD is back to normal by Age

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.540
of Ultron next year.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.050
Marvel does a great job with continuity, so
I don’t think that will be the case.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.050
Now it’s your turn though.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.370
Let me know what your favorite moments were
and how long you think it will be before SHIELD

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.370
completely repairs itself.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.160
So here’s my review and then I’ll talk
sequels and marvelverse overlapping

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.720
I gave the movie a solid A as a follow up
to to Avengers.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:46.640
It’s really the most direct sequel to an
Avengers movie there’s been.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:52.040
Iron Man and Thor always had very little interaction
with SHIELD at an organizational level.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:56.620
But Captain America has basically been working
for SHIELD ever since the Avengers.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.300
I loved how they paired him with Black Widow
in this movie.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:04.040
It’s funny to see how the tone of the story
changes based on which Avengers are together.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.680
This movie was all about identity but it didn’t
completely answer the biggest question it

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:09.680
asked.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.710
Who Am I?

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:14.500
Which is why we’ll all go see that next
movie with those characters, which is Age

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.500
of Ultron.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:20.800
I didn’t feel they crammed in too much expositional
bits for all those other movies, which was

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:21.800
great.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.590
And how about that Doctor Strange name drop
from Sitwell.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:30.700
May he rest in pieces.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:35.750
One of the best things about it was how different
it was from Thor or Iron Man or even the last

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.270
Captain America movie.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.080
The first movie was a period War Drama.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.740
This was a political thriller, that had amazing
action.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.880
I think them doing it as a thriller also made
them work that much harder at the dialogue

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.170
and it paid off brilliantly.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:54.050
Punching and kicking stuff is a lot of fun
to watch, but I’m not 10 years old anymore,

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.870
I need interesting characters to keep me watching.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:01.530
And just like in my top moments, Black Widow,
the cap and Anthony Mackie were all great.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:06.050
Nick Fury had about as many lines as he usually
gets, Samuel L. Jackson can do a lot with

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.050
just a look.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.050
He doesn’t need long speeches.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:11.500
The only thing I thought could have been better
would have been cutting out Larry Sanders,

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.720
I don’t know why, of all things to call
back to in old movies, they used him.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.720
There was also the bit with Arnim Zola.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.571
Logically, if he was AI and was affecting
all of SHIELD’s systems, why didn’t he

00:07:26.571 --> 00:07:29.160
move his consciousness to the cloud.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.560
Back in the 70s pre internet yes, he would
have been stuck in that basement, but now

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:37.790
in the age of information and distributed
processing, why didn’t he live on servers

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.180
all over the globe?

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.450
I think the answer is, because they want to
save something that big for Ultron in Avengers

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.450
2.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:47.080
But let me know what your final thoughts on
the movie were, love it or hate it.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.910
What we really need to talk about now is how
everything that happened affects what’s

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:51.970
coming next.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:56.490
Namely Age of Ultron, Agents of SHIELD season
2 and Captain America 3.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:01.310
So right off the bat, let’s talk about Arnim
Zola’s algorithm as it applies to Ultron.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:05.100
The algorithm was designed to evaluate the
sum total of everyone’s lives on the planet

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.710
and assess them as threats.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:11.040
Ultron in the comics decides that humans in
general are too big of a threat to be allowed

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.420
to live, thus his kill all humans mission
begins.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.950
Does this mean that Arnim Zola’s Algorithm
is going to evolve into Ultron?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.840
No, at least not completely.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:28.150
The rumor is that Ultron will be an AI created
for the military that just becomes self aware

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.790
and does what machines do, create the most
efficient system possible.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:35.330
And humans, being fundamentally flawed, aren’t
part of that equation.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:39.629
But the idea of the algorithm and the way
it evaluated humans as threats was a spiritual

00:08:39.629 --> 00:08:43.990
not literal prequel to Ultron.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.240
Quicksilver and Scarlet Witch too, look like
they had the same type of brainwashing treatment

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.460
Bucky got.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:53.639
They actually be fighting the Avengers the
first time they meet, but eventually they’ll

00:08:53.639 --> 00:08:57.190
get folded into the roster and hopefully go
on to appear in Avengers 3.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:01.500
I loved how Von Strucker said he was basically
going to throw other Hydra teams under the

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:05.199
bus to throw SHIELD off his scent.

00:09:05.199 --> 00:09:10.980
Captain America 3 though has a lot of interesting
directions it can take.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:15.830
There have been a lot of rumors that they’ll
do a version of the death of Captain America

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.120
story and a now rehabilitated Bucky will take
his place temporarily.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:25.670
I already did a video for potential stories
that I’ll post a link to at the end of this

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:26.670
video.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:32.209
Of all the other Marvel things happening,
Agents of SHIELD is in the weirdest place.

00:09:32.209 --> 00:09:35.699
After season 1, SHIELD will basically not
exist for a while.

00:09:35.699 --> 00:09:41.829
So does that mean if the show gets a season
2, they’ll be on the hunt for HYDRA remnants

00:09:41.829 --> 00:09:44.379
or helping to rebuild SHIELD?

00:09:44.379 --> 00:09:48.959
Now that Cobie Smulders is done with How I
Met Your Mother, I’m hoping she joins the

00:09:48.959 --> 00:09:50.980
cast of SHIELD.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:55.920
She’s like one movie behind Black Widow
in terms of character development.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:01.170
You start as window dressing, then you get
a background part, then you get center stage.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:06.620
Let me know if you want to see Maria Hill
become part of Agents of SHIELD full time.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.850
So in other news, more SHIELD Winter Soldier
crossover next week.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.529
Be sure to subscribe to get my video.

00:10:12.529 --> 00:10:15.480
I’ll also be posting my Arrow Deathstroke
Q&amp;A later today.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.751
In the meantime click here to learn more about
Avengers 2 and click here for my top 5 stories

00:10:20.751 --> 00:10:21.751
for Captain America 3.

00:10:21.751 --> 00:10:24.370
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.220
High Fives!

